# VEdit Environment Configuration Example
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# VEdit is a 100% in-browser, client-side video editor powered by
# WebAssembly (FFmpeg WASM), WebCodecs, WebGPU, and Transformers.js.
#
# No server credentials, database keys, or third-party API tokens are required.
# All media ingestion, AI processing, and video rendering executes locally on device.
# -------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional: Base URL for custom self-hosted FFmpeg WASM core assets (defaults to public CDN if unset)
# VITE_FFMPEG_CORE_URL=https://unpkg.com/@ffmpeg/core@0.12.10/dist/esm

# Optional: Enable verbose client debug logging in development mode (true | false)
# VITE_DEBUG_LOGGING=false
